sform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 1}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 153.03 0) translate(22.74,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.48 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Psi_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Psi_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 168.9)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 33.67 0) translate(9.42,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.46 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>2</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 2}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 86.17 0) translate(22.36,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.1 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.17em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 220.65 0) translate(19.48,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -5.22 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="10.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces Z}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 215.47)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 33.67 0) translate(9.42,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -3.46 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.5em;--ltx-fo-height:0.64em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="8.92" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 8.92)" width="6.92"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces 3}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 86.17 0) translate(22.36,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.1 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.17em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 50.12 5.76 L 50.12 27.56"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 -1.0 0.0 50.12 5.76)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 2.71 C 0.95 2.71 1.72 2.1 1.72 1.36 C 1.72 0.61 0.95 0 0 0"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 50.12 27.84)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -1.14 -43.08 L 34.95 -18.08"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-0.822 -0.56949 -0.56949 0.822 -1.14 -43.08)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 2.71 C 0.95 2.71 1.72 2.1 1.72 1.36 C 1.72 0.61 0.95 0 0 0"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.822 0.56949 -0.56949 0.822 35.17 -17.92)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 101.41 -44.68 L 65.29 -18.55"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.81013 -0.58624 -0.58624 -0.81013 101.41 -44.68)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 2.71 C 0.95 2.71 1.72 2.1 1.72 1.36 C 1.72 0.61 0.95 0 0 0"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(-0.81013 0.58624 -0.58624 -0.81013 65.06 -18.38)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M -17.11 -87.37 L -17.11 -65.57"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 -1.0 0.0 -17.11 -87.37)"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 2.71 C 0.95 2.71 1.72 2.1 1.72 1.36 C 1.72 0.61 0.95 0 0 0"></path></g><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" transform="matrix(0.0 1.0 -1.0 0.0 -17.11 -65.29)"><path style="fill:none" d="M -2.88 3.32 C -2.35 1.33 -1.18 0.39 0 0 C -1.18 -0.39 -2.35 -1.33 -2.88 -3.32"></path></g></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F1.pic2" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="244.07" overflow="visible" style="vertical-align:-122.03px" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 83.52 244.07" width="83.52"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,244.07) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(41.76,0) translate(0,122.04)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -41.76 -116.97)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 244.07)"><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 14.67)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(41.76,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -35.8 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.18em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.14em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.49" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="71.61"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="S4.F1.pic2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath">our <math id="S4.F1.pic2.m1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math> order</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 52.74)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 27.32 0) translate(14.44,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.48 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Psi_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Psi_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 99.31)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 27.32 0) translate(14.44,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.48 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.23em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.97"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Psi_{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Psi_{1}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 145.88)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 27.7 0) translate(14.06,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.1 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.17em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 192.44)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 27.7 0) translate(14.06,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -8.1 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:1.17em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.15em;font-size:10pt;" height="11.53" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="16.2"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{3}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces\Sigma_{3}}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g class="ltx_tikzmatrix_row" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 239.01)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_tikzmatrix_col ltx_nopad_l ltx_nopad_r" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 30.59 0) translate(11.18,0) matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -5.22 0)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:0.75em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="10.44"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><math id="S4.F1.pic2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\lx@inpgf@ignorespaces Z}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 37.52 L 0 61.88"></path></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -9.04 L 0 15.31"></path></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -55.61 L 0 -31.26"></path></g><g stroke-width="0.39998pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -102.17 L 0 -77.82"></path></g></g></svg></span></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1. </span>Two partial orders on the genus <math id="S4.F1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> strata</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The table on the left of Figure <a href="#S4.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 4.4. Genus 
          
            7
          
         tetragonal curves ‣ 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> lists the codimensions of strata (computed with (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1. Pair splitting loci on 
          
            
              
              H
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  4
                  ,
                  g ‣ 3. Splitting Loci ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)). It also
indicates the partial order of which strata lie in the closure of others, which can be seen by considering (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3. Splitting Loci ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>). This should be contrasted with the our partial ordering <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math>, which is pictured on the right.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmthm8" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmthm8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 4.8</span></span><span id="S4.Thmthm8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmthm8.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The Chow ring <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}))</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by CE classes. Hence, all classes supported on <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7}^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7}^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> are tautological on <math id="S4.Thmthm8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S4.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We implement Strategy <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1. Strategy ‣ 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>, starting at the bottom of the partial ordering. By (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>), we have</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z=\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{2})=\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z=\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{2})=\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The second equality follows because a genus <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>7</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">7</annotation></semantics></math> curve cannot possess maps to <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of degrees <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>4</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">4</annotation></semantics></math>, otherwise it would map to <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{P}^{1}\times\mathbb{P}^{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{P}^{1}\times\mathbb{P}^{1}</annotation></semantics></math> with image a curve of bidegree <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(3,4)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(3,4)</annotation></semantics></math>, which has genus <math id="S4.SS4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>6</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Next, we claim that, modulo classes supported on <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>, the fundamental class of <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressible in terms of CE classes.
To see this, observe that <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{3}=\Sigma_{(2,3,5)}(\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{3}=\Sigma_{(2,3,5)}(\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\codim\Sigma_{3}=3=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(2,3,5)))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>codim</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\codim\Sigma_{3}=3=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(2,3,5))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the claim follows from Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3. Splitting Loci ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>. By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4.2. Chow rings of very unbalanced splitting strata ‣ 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> (<a href="#S4.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4.2. Chow rings of very unbalanced splitting strata ‣ 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we see <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\Sigma_{3})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\Sigma_{3})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by the restrictions of CE classes, so by the push-pull formula, every class supported on on <math id="S4.SS4.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{3}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{3}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus Z</annotation></semantics></math> is expressible in terms of CE classes, i.e. is tautological.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, modulo classes supported on <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>, we claim that the fundamental class of <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is expressible in terms of CE classes. To see this, observe that <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{2}=\Sigma_{(2,4,4)}(\mathcal{E})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{2}=\Sigma_{(2,4,4)}(\mathcal{E})</annotation></semantics></math> and</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\codim\Sigma_{2}=2=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(2,4,4)))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>codim</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>h</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ℙ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\codim\Sigma_{2}=2=h^{1}(\mathbb{P}^{1},\mathcal{E}nd(\mathcal{O}(2,4,4))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p6.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p6.2.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, the claim again follows from Lemma <a href="#S3.Thmthm7" title="Lemma 3.7. ‣ 3. Splitting Loci ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.7</span></a>. By Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmthm3" title="Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4.2. Chow rings of very unbalanced splitting strata ‣ 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> (<a href="#S4.I2.i1" title="item 1 ‣ Lemma 4.3. ‣ 4.2. Chow rings of very unbalanced splitting strata ‣ 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>), we see <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\Sigma_{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\Sigma_{2})</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by restrictions of CE classes. Using the push-pull formula, along with the previous paragraph, we see that every class supported on <math id="S4.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{2}\cup\Sigma_{3}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mi>Z</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{2}\cup\Sigma_{3}\subset\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus Z</annotation></semantics></math> is tautological.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Proposition
<a href="#S2.Thmthm9" title="Proposition 2.9. ‣ 2.1. The Casnati–Ekedahl structure theorem ‣ 2. Hurwitz Schemes and the Tautological Ring ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.9</span></a>, we know <math id="S4.SS4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\Psi)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\Psi)</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by tautological classes. Putting this together with the above, we find that <math id="S4.SS4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A^{*}(\Psi\cup\Sigma_{2}\cup\Sigma_{3})=A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>A</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msub><mo>∖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>β</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A^{*}(\Psi\cup\Sigma_{2}\cup\Sigma_{3})=A^{*}(\mathcal{H}_{4,7}\smallsetminus\beta^{-1}(\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}))</annotation></semantics></math> is generated by tautological classes. Applying Theorem <a href="#S2.Thmthm4" title="Theorem 2.4. ‣ 2. Hurwitz Schemes and the Tautological Ring ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a>, every class supported on <math id="S4.SS4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7}^{4}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7}^{4}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> is tautological in <math id="S4.SS4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn></msub><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7}\smallsetminus\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. classes supported on <math id="S4.SS4.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mn>7</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}_{7}^{3}</annotation></semantics></math> are known to be tautological (see (<a href="#S1.E1" title="In (1) An easy start ‣ 1. Introduction ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1.1</span></a>)), so the result follows.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.5. </span>Genus <math id="S4.SS5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>8</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">8</annotation></semantics></math> tetragonal curves</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Using (<a href="#S4.E3" title="In 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a>) – (<a href="#S4.E9" title="In 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.9</span></a>), there are five allowed splitting types for the CE bundles, which give rise to the following stratification of <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{4,8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{4,8}</annotation></semantics></math>. Again, we label a stratum with a <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> if it is contained within <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi</annotation></semantics></math>, equivalently if <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2e_{1}-f_{2}\geq-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0em">≥</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2e_{1}-f_{2}\geq-1</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<ol id="S4.I6" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S4.I6.ix1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S4.I6.ix1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.ix1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I6.ix1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I6.ix1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(3,4,4),F=(5,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(3,4,4),F=(5,6)</annotation></semantics></math>: generic stratum; the associated scroll is smooth.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I6.ix2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S4.I6.ix2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.ix2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I6.ix2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I6.ix2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(3,4,4),F=(4,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(3,4,4),F=(4,7)</annotation></semantics></math>: associated scroll is smooth, <math id="S4.I6.ix2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> unbalanced.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I6.ix3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S4.I6.ix3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.ix3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I6.ix3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I6.ix3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(3,3,5),F=(5,6)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(3,3,5),F=(5,6)</annotation></semantics></math>: associated scroll is smooth, <math id="S4.I6.ix3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>E</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E</annotation></semantics></math> unbalanced.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I6.ix4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S4.I6.ix4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Sigma_{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Σ</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Sigma_{3}</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.ix4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I6.ix4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I6.ix4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(2,4,5),F=(4,7)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>7</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(2,4,5),F=(4,7)</annotation></semantics></math>: associated scroll is a cone over <math id="S4.I6.ix4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{F}_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝔽</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{F}_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Bielliptic curves are a proper closed subvariety here, see <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, Theorem 2.3]</cite>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I6.ix5" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">(<math id="S4.I6.ix5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Z</annotation></semantics></math>)</span> 
<div id="S4.I6.ix5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I6.ix5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I6.ix5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=(1,5,5),F=(2,9)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=(1,5,5),F=(2,9)</annotation></semantics></math>: stratum of hyperelliptic curves (see (<a href="#S4.E5" title="In 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.5</span></a>)).</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The table on the left of Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 4.5. Genus 
          
            8
          
         tetragonal curves ‣ 4. The Tetragonal Locus ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> lists the codimension of strata (see (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.1. Pair splitting loci on 
          
            
              
              H
              
                
                  
                  
                  
                
                
                  4
                  ,
                  g ‣ 3. Splitting Loci ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.3</span></a>)) and
indicates which strata are in the closure of others, which can be seen by considering (<a href="#S3.E2" title="In 3. Splitting Loci ‣ The Chow Rings of the Moduli Spaces of Curves of Genus 7, 8, and 9" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a>). This should be contrasted with our partial ordering <math id="S4.SS5.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq</annotation></semantics></math>, which is pictured on the right.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure">
